 is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe  maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-1)I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-1)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$  \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{min}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198443 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6115493b-482c-5360-8d19-52582228e21d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Where the Extrema of a Quadratic Form Is Attained on the Unit Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d9e2ab8-f0d5-5abe-b74e-db6a46609bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492276} {:answer/id #uuid "208b060c-d7f6-5417-9e03-796577024e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492282} {:answer/id #uuid "96521b38-e0b7-58e6-b1db-eeed